{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/997684-question-about-contracts-and-kith-bonuses","id":997684,"title":"Question About Contracts and Kith Bonuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T07:44:07-07:00","id":997684,"title":"Question About Contracts and Kith Bonuses","content":"Hello :-)<br /> <br /> Do Kith Bonuses add to Contract rolls? For example:<br /> <br /> Vainglory: Roll: Presence + Intimidation + Wyrd<br /> Venombite: Bonus: Add Wyrd to all Intimidation checks<br /> Merit: Potent Kith: Add Merit Rating to Wyrd for purposes of Kith Blessing<br /> <br /> Result: Vainglory: Roll: Presence + Intimidation + Wyrd + Wyrd + Potent Kith?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:51:53-07:00","id":997691,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the answer will be no.<br /> <br /> Out-of-Character, because that's kinda broken and not what the writers want.<br /> <br /> In-character, because the roll to activate a contract using a skill isn't actually a &quot;skill check&quot;. It's magic based on one's affinity to the concept of, in this case, intimidation. Being physically scary doesn't help here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:06:42-07:00","id":997700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/997684-question-about-contracts-and-kith-bonuses?p=997691#post997691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out-of-Character, because that's kinda broken and not what the writers want.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/997684-question-about-contracts-and-kith-bonuses?p=997691#post997691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-character, because the roll to activate a contract using a skill isn't actually a &quot;skill check&quot;. It's magic based on one's affinity to the concept of, in this case, intimidation. Being physically scary doesn't help here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely disagree with this however. Especially in regards to Vainglory, being physically intimidating (not necessarily &quot;scary&quot; per se) absolutely is a large part of the effectiveness of the contract. You're using your talents of Intimidation, augmented by your force of personality, and backed by the magic of the Wyrd to affect people in intimidating ways. In Character, it seems to fit quite well to me.<br /> <br /> But as far as balance issues go, yeah, you're probably right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:11:21-07:00","id":997707,"title":"","content":"I'm sure the actual writers could come up with a better in-game justification for it working the way they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:32:59-08:00","id":999764,"title":"","content":"Unless the kith bonus is directly gives you a skill or attribute equal to Wyrd it doesn't work. Skill checks are explicitly different than power uses. It doesn't matter that you are using an intimidation power, you are bypassing the skill use by using said power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T08:20:13-08:00","id":1000277,"title":"","content":"In that case, would the Witchtooth kith's effect of granting the 8-again quality to all Occult rolls apply to any Contracts with the Occult skill required? There are barely any contracts that use Occult, so it somewhat balances out in that aspect. Just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}